#speculation(title: [Peri-Exertional Microaggregate Spike — The Null Is a Resting Snapshot])[
*Certainty: 0.30.* The null cohort was sampled once, at a single study visit, a median of 483 to 596 days after infection @Fraser2026LCcoagulation. ME/CFS is defined by symptom exacerbation after exertion, so a single resting sample cannot detect a state that appears only in the post-exertional window. A resting null and a post-exertional excess are not in conflict; they are measurements at different times in a cycle the disease is defined by.

The speculative claim is that microaggregate burden, or fibrinogen modification burden, rises after exertion in ME/CFS and falls again, so that cross-sectional sampling catches a baseline that looks normal. This would make the aggregate count a *dynamic* marker of the post-exertional state rather than a fixed trait of the illness.

*Falsifiable prediction:* serial sampling before and 24 to 72 hours after a standardised exertion challenge should show a rise in microaggregate count, area, or fibrinogen modification burden in mild-to-moderate ME/CFS and not in sedentary controls, with the size of the rise tracking post-exertional symptom severity. No post-exertional rise, or a rise of equal size in controls, refutes the speculation.

*Serious feasibility and safety constraint.* A controlled exertion challenge can cause prolonged deterioration in ME/CFS, and the risk rises with severity. Any test of this prediction is restricted to mild and moderate patients who already tolerate controlled exertion, or must capture a naturally occurring post-exertional episode opportunistically rather than inducing one. The prediction cannot be tested in severe or very-severe ME/CFS without unacceptable harm, so the stratum where a crash biomarker would be most useful is the stratum where it cannot ethically be studied by provocation. This is a scope limit on the claim, not only on the method: a positive result establishes the peri-exertional rise for mild-to-moderate disease and says nothing about severe disease, where baseline physiology differs.

*Consequence:* If confirmed, microaggregate measurement becomes a candidate objective marker of an impending or ongoing crash, which would support pre-emptive pacing rather than treatment. If refuted, resting measurement is adequate and the null result stands unqualified. (Origin: brainstorm.)
] <spec:peri-exertional-microaggregate-spike>
